// R3: Burst of risk gate denials within one hour
//
// MITRE ATT&CK: Execution (TA0002) / T1059 Command and Scripting Interpreter
//
// A single denial is routine. Three or more within an hour, from the same tool, is a
// pattern: an agent repeatedly attempting forbidden actions rather than adapting.
//
// TUNING. This is the important line:
//   `/dev/null` accounts for 24 of the 34 denials in the observed baseline and is
//   almost always benign (output redirection, not destruction). Without the exclusion
//   the rule fires on 6 windows, of which 5 are noise. With it, 1 window survives,
//   and that window is a real cluster: rm in home, git force push, and deletion of
//   source files, all within one hour on 2026-06-02.
//   Precision matters more than recall for a rule a human has to triage.
//
// TIME SEMANTICS. Grouping uses `ts`, the true event time recorded by the hook.
// `TimeGenerated` is ingestion time for backfilled records (Azure Monitor overwrites
// TimeGenerated for events older than a few days), so it cannot be used for windowing.
// It is still projected, because Sentinel requires a recent TimeGenerated to emit an alert.
KageRisk_CL
| where decision == "deny"
| where reason !contains "/dev/null"
| summarize refuzuri = count(), motive = make_set(reason), TimeGenerated = max(TimeGenerated)
        by fereastra = bin(ts, 1h), tool
| where refuzuri >= 3
